cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this atlas, please cite the repository, the release tag and the version below,
  together with the underlying data resources (RCSB PDB, GPCRdb, UniProt). This is a pre-release
  beta: it has no DOI and it is not a curated or independently validated resource.
title: "Class A GPCR Structure-Ligand Contact and Interface Atlas"
abstract: >-
  Atlas of 1358 experimentally determined Class A (rhodopsin-like) GPCR structures across 11
  GPCRdb major families. Contains exact minimum heavy-atom receptor-ligand contacts at 4.0, 4.5
  and 5.0 Angstrom computed from deposited coordinates, residue-level GPCRdb generic numbering,
  site-class-aware aggregation over 727 analysis units, and measurements over 8 core Class A
  motifs. Small-molecule pockets and receptor-polymer interfaces are treated as separate analysis
  objects and never share a denominator. The atlas contains no potency, affinity or functional
  pathway activity data. Scientific claims have not been reviewed by a human curator: 189 review
  items remain open, and public-beta pooled summaries are review-gated.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Karakaya"
    given-names: "Muhammed Fatih"
    affiliation: "Cancer Signaling Laboratory, Boğaziçi University"
    email: "edu.mfatih@gmail.com"
version: "0.1.0-beta.1"
date-released: "2026-08-05"
repository-code: "https://github.com/karakayafm/class-a-gpcr-atlas"
url: "https://karakayafm.github.io/class-a-gpcr-atlas/"
license-url: "https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0"
keywords:
  - GPCR
  - Class A GPCR
  - structural biology
  - protein-ligand contacts
  - GPCRdb generic numbering
  - molecular visualization
